75	10	simple-41100	Philosophy and religion	65.8	simple	Occam's razor	10949672	Occam's razor (or Ockham's razor) is a principle from philosophy. Suppose an event has two possible explanations. Occam's razor says that the explanation with the fewest assumptions is usually correct. Another way of saying it is that, the more assumptions you have to make, the more unlikely an explanation is.
